\begin{theorem}\label{thm: independent_rate}
Under \cref{ass: Alex2022}, \cref{ass: independent_DCT}, \cref{ass: independent_step}, and \cref{ass: independent_rate}, for any $\delta>0$, we have with probability at least $1-\delta,$ for any $T>0$, the following bound on the expected gradient of the final output under the true parameter $\theta^c$  
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] If the step size satisfies $a_t=\frac{a}{\sqrt{T}}$, $\forall t \leq T$, for some constant $a<\frac{\sqrt{T}}{L_h}$, then 
